Silicon Valley is quietly running on Chinese open source AI models. Cursor confirmed last month that Composer 2 is built on Moonshot's Kimi K2.5. Cognition's SWE-1.6 model is likely post-trained on Zhipu's GLM. Shopify saved $5M a year by switching to Alibaba’s Qwen model, and Airbnb CEO Brian Chesky has stated: "We rely a lot on Qwen. It's very good, fast, and cheap."

Now, Zhipu has released GLM-5.1, an open source model that performs almost as well as Opus on coding benchmarks.

